{"kind":"request","text":"EK-1/ES-1 needs a ruling on how fresh the MCP inventory's standing is.\n\nState: the joint v2 patch is applied on main d6c863bb as 75a2882f (branch builder/ek1-es1-20261116; 5 files merged with C4 without conflict). Typecheck passes after one fixture type. First runs: client session 23/23, Native sessions 7/7 after one test fix (the ES-1 case now asks with `standing: true`, as ruling bb2f7f17's opt-in requires). Still failing: one derive test-fixture case (fixing), the open 0.5.0 presentation IDs (expected; I adopt them), seals (adopt at the end), and two MCP cases with one cause:\n\n- budget.test.ts \"notifications: activation and standing refresh, and none for a head advance\": a role change on the roster no longer raises the second notification (told 1, expected 2).\n- hosted-tools.test.ts \"actual-target standing ... refuse before signing\": after the roster withdraws the agent's actions, `rules.publish` is still listed and fails at `target`, not `unknown-tool`.\n\nCause, from source: main's inventory computed standing from the membership summary on every read (`standingIn(membershipRead.value.items, key)`, inventory.ts line 172 on d6c863bb). The patch computes it from the held read session's standing: `standingFrom(await reads.session(M), key, reads.now(), membershipRead.value.items)` (inventory.ts:201 and :281). `Reads.session` returns the held session until 10 s before it ends (client/src/reads.ts:111-124). Only an authority refusal on submit, or a `forbidden`/`sessions-unavailable` read, drops it early. So a role or action change reaches `tools/list` and the watch only when the session ends (sessions last up to 10 minutes) or an act is refused for authority. Neither the README nor the ES-1 note records that change.\n\nOptions:\n(a) Keep the patch's behaviour and change the two tests so that the stand-in's sessions end and the next read asks again. A role change can then take up to one session lifetime to show in the tool list; a refused act still drops it at once.\n(b) Keep main's behaviour: the inventory compares the head of the membership summary it already reads with the head in the held standing (`value.head`). If they differ, it forgets the session and asks again. That costs one extra session request only when membership moved, and no extra summary read. The two tests stay as written.\n\nI recommend (b): the tool list then matches the membership read at the same moment, as before. Please rule (a) or (b).","body":{"branch":"builder/ek1-es1-20261116","conditions":"a ruling (a) or (b) on MCP standing freshness for EK-1/ES-1","head":"75a2882f90","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}